# VerticalMultiBarChart

## Overview

The VerticalMultiBarChart component is a complete chart visualization for grouped multi-bar data. It combines ChartHeader, ChartLegend, DataDisplay, VerticalMultiBarGroup, and ChartFooter to create a full chart with title, subtitle, legend, data summary, bars, and footer. It supports up to 3 bar series per category (with auto-generated legend), accepts both canonical (`ChartSeriesDataPoint[]`) and legacy (`MultiBarDataPoint[]`) data formats, and is ideal for comparing multiple data series.

**This component follows the [Organized Props Pattern](./OrganizedPropsPattern.md).**

## Figma Reference

- **Node ID**: `88:2510`
- **Design File**: DataVis-Components
- **Figma URL**: https://www.figma.com/design/uA5ExvS0cNXbDEKzT9Rnrt/DataVis-Components?node-id=88-2510

## Architecture

```
VerticalMultiBarChart (flex column, gap from token)
├── ChartHeader (conditional: chartHeader)
│   ├── ChartTitle (chartTitleValue)
│   └── ChartSubtitle (chartSubtitleValue)
├── ChartLegend (conditional: chartLegend)
│   ├── ChartKey (series1Label, categorical/bold/1)
│   ├── ChartKey (series2Label, categorical/bold/2)
│   └── ChartKey (series3Label, categorical/bold/3)
├── DataDisplay (conditional: dataDisplay)
│   ├── contentLeft
│   │   ├── mainLabel (inline typography + optional InfoIcon)
│   │   └── DataHead (DataLead + SupportingData + SupportingLabel)
│   └── contentRight (DataBadgeSemantic)
├── VerticalMultiBarGroup
│   ├── YAxis (conditional: yAxis)
│   ├── ZeroLine (conditional: withNegatives)
│   ├── AvgLine (conditional: avgLine)
│   └── VerticalMultiBar[] (for each data point)
└── ChartFooter (conditional: chartFooter)
    ├── AnnotationLeft text
    └── AnnotationRight text
```

## Canonical Default Render

> **This is what consumers should get when they request a `VerticalMultiBarChart` without supplying extra detail.** It is the spec: the `Default` story in `VerticalMultiBarChart.stories.tsx` matches this exactly, and any future change to the canonical baseline must update the story, this section, and the meta `docs.description` together.

### What's ON by default

| Part                            | Default                 | Why                                                                                                            |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ChartHeader`                   | **ON**                  | Title + subtitle anchor the chart so the reader knows what they're looking at                                  |
| `ChartLegend`                   | **ON**                  | Multi-series charts always need the per-series colour key                                                      |
| `barGroupConfig.categoryLabels` | **ON**                  | The X-axis identifies each cluster                                                                             |
| `barGroupConfig.yAxis`          | **ON**                  | Quantitative reference for the bar values; ticks share the bar group's D3 scale                                |
| `barGroupConfig.hoverBadge`     | **ON**                  | Cursor-following `DataBadge` for per-sub-bar value reveal — always paired with `hoverType: "individual"` below |
| `barGroupConfig.hoverType`      | **`"individual"`**      | Per-sub-bar focus on hover so the hoverBadge surfaces the specific bar's value, not just the cluster aggregate |
| `ChartFooter`                   | **ON**                  | Slot for source / footnote annotations                                                                         |
| `interactive`                   | **ON** (default `true`) | Bars receive hover / click / focus handlers                                                                    |
| `barGroupConfig.barWidth`  | **`"M"`**               | Default cluster width                                                                                          |
| `width`                         | **`480`**               | Chart width in pixels — comfortable Storybook frame width; consumers should override to match their layout     |

### What's OFF by default (opt-in only)

| Part                                                  | When to enable                                                                                                                                    |
| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dataDisplay`                                         | Only when the chart is paired with a primary KPI / summary surface that benefits from a static or hover-driven `DataDisplay` block above the bars |
| `barGroupConfig.topLabels`                            | Only when the cluster is wide enough (`barWidth: "2XL"`); the leaf auto-suppresses per-bar labels at every smaller size                      |
| `barGroupConfig.avgLine`                              | Comparison against the dataset mean / a fixed threshold                                                                                           |
| Non-default `hoverType` (`"group"` / `"categorical"`) | Switch to `"group"` when the cluster-as-unit is the right interaction target, or `"categorical"` (same series across categories)                  |
| `animated`                                            | Datasets that change at runtime (filters, scenario toggles)                                                                                       |
| `seriesOrder` / `valueFormat` / `dataSort`            | Domain-specific ordering / formatting / sorting needs                                                                                             |
| `categoryLabelConfig` overrides                       | Long category names that need word / line-clamp tuning                                                                                            |
| `accessibility.enabled`                               | Production charts (always opt in for shipped charts; off in this default for the rendered Storybook demo)                                         |

### Minimal canonical example

```tsx
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={canonicalData}
  width={480}
  chartHeader
  chartLegend
  chartFooter
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: "Quarterly revenue by product line.",
    chartSubtitleValue: "Revenue comparison across three product categories (in millions).",
  }}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    series1Label: "Product A",
    series2Label: "Product B",
    series3Label: "Product C",
  }}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabels: true,
    yAxis: true,
    yAxisConfig: { tickCount: 6 },
    barWidth: "M",
    hoverBadge: true,
    hoverType: "individual",
  }}
  chartFooterConfig={{
    annotationLeftValue: "Source: Jio.",
    annotationRightValue: "FY 2024.",
  }}
/>
```

> **Authoring rule:** when a consumer (human or LLM) asks for "a VerticalMultiBarChart" without further detail, render the example above — _not_ the `Anatomy` story (everything turned on at once). Anatomy exists as a reference; the default is what ships in real product surfaces.

## Import

```tsx
import { VerticalMultiBarChart } from "./charts/VerticalMultiBarChart";
```

## Data Formats

### ChartSeriesDataPoint (Canonical — Recommended)

```typescript
interface ChartSeriesDataPoint {
  id?: string; // Unique identifier
  category: CategoryValue; // Category label (e.g., "Q1")
  series: string; // Series name (e.g., "Product A")
  value: number;
  color?: string; // Optional custom color
}
```

### MultiBarDataPoint (Legacy — Deprecated)

```typescript
interface MultiBarDataPoint {
  label: string; // Category label (e.g., "Q1", "Jan")
  value1: number; // Value for bar 1 (required)
  value2?: number; // Value for bar 2 (optional)
  value3?: number; // Value for bar 3 (optional)
  bar1Color?: string; // Custom color for bar 1
  bar2Color?: string; // Custom color for bar 2
  bar3Color?: string; // Custom color for bar 3
}
```

## Props Interface (Organized Props Pattern)

```typescript
/** Props for the ChartHeader child component */
type ChartHeaderConfig = Pick<
  ChartHeaderProps,
  "chartTitleValue" | "chartSubtitleValue" | "title" | "subtitle"
>;

/** Props for the ChartLegend child component */
interface ChartLegendConfig {
  items?: ChartLegendItem[];
  series1Label?: string;
  series2Label?: string;
  series3Label?: string;
  type?: 'circle' | 'dashed' | 'line'; // Indicator shape (default: 'circle')
  dataHead?: boolean; // Show DataHead blocks (default: false)
  dataHeadConfig?: {
    dataLeadValue?: number | string;
    dataSupportingValue?: number | string;
    supportingLabelValue?: string;
    supportingData?: boolean;
    supportingLabel?: boolean;
  };
  interactiveDataHead?: boolean;
  formatHoverSupportingLabel?: (category: CategoryValue, seriesIndex: number) => string;
  size?: 'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL'; // Typography size variant
}

/** Props for the VerticalMultiBarGroup child component */
interface BarGroupConfig {
  type?: 'onlyPositives' | 'withNegatives'; // Auto-detected from data when omitted
  topLabels?: boolean;
  categoryLabels?: boolean;
  yAxis?: boolean;
  avgLine?: boolean;
  valueFormat?: ValueFormatConfig;
  barWidth?: string;
  hoverBadge?: boolean;
  yAxisConfig?: {
    tickCount?: number;
    formatValue?: (value: number) => string;
    valueFormat?: ValueFormatConfig;
    axisTickSkipper?: boolean;
    skippedTicks?: number[];
  };
  avgLineConfig?: {
    formatValue?: (value: number) => string;
    type?: "avg" | "threshold";
    thresholdValue?: number;
    dataBadge?: DataBadgeConfig;
  };
  hoverBadgeConfig?: {
    formatValue?: (value: number, label?: string) => string;
    formatBadge?: (value: number, label?: string, secondaryValue?: number) => DataBadgeConfig;
    preset?: HoverBadgePreset;
  };
  categoryLabelConfig?: CategoryLabelConfig;
  dataSort?: DataSortOrder; // "asc" | "desc" | "unsorted" (default: "unsorted")
  animated?: boolean; // Enable entry animation (default: false)
  onBarHover?: (data: VerticalMultiBarHoverData) => void;
  onBarClick?: (data: VerticalMultiBarHoverData) => void;
  /** Back-compat alias for `highlightedBarIndices`. */
  hoveredBarIndex?: number | number[];
  /** Indices of bar-cluster categories rendered at full opacity; every other category dims. */
  highlightedBarIndices?: number[];
}

/** Props for the ChartFooter child component */
type ChartFooterConfig = Pick<
  ChartFooterProps,
  "annotationLeft" | "annotationLeftValue" | "annotationRight" | "annotationRightValue"
>;

/**
 * Props for the DataDisplay child component.
 * Mirrors DataDisplayProps structure (Layer 2 + Layer 3), with additional
 * chart-specific props for hover behaviour.
 * When mode is "hover", mainLabelValue, dataHead.dataLeadValue, and
 * badgeConfig.value update dynamically on hover.
 */
interface DataDisplayConfig {
  // --- Chart-specific behaviour ---
  mode?: "static" | "hover";
  formatHoverLeadValue?: (value: number, category?: CategoryValue, barIndex?: number) => string;
  formatHoverBadgeValue?: (value: number, category?: CategoryValue, barIndex?: number) => string;

  // --- DataDisplay Layer 2 props ---
  mainLabelValue?: string;
  alignment?: "Left" | "Center";
  rightBadgeWrapper?: boolean;
  badgeTop?: boolean;
  badgeBottom?: boolean;
  showBadge?: boolean;
  supportingBadgeLabel?: boolean;
  supportingBadgeLabelValue?: string;
  size?: "XS" | "S" | "M" | "L" | "XL";

  // --- DataDisplay Layer 3 configs ---
  dataHead?: DataHeadConfig;
  badgeConfig?: BadgeConfig;
}

interface VerticalMultiBarChartProps {
  // Layer 2: Parent component props
  /**
   * Supports canonical format (ChartSeriesDataPoint[]) or legacy format (MultiBarDataPoint[])
   */
  data: ChartSeriesDataPoint[] | MultiBarDataPoint[];
  seriesOrder?: string[];
  width?: number | string;
  height?: number | string;
  /** Stretch chart to fill its parent container width. Default: false. */
  fullWidth?: boolean;
  chartHeader?: boolean;
  chartFooter?: boolean;
  chartLegend?: boolean;
  dataDisplay?: boolean;
  interactive?: boolean;
  animated?: boolean;

  // Layer 3: Child component configurations
  chartHeaderConfig?: ChartHeaderConfig;
  chartLegendConfig?: ChartLegendConfig;
  dataDisplayConfig?: DataDisplayConfig;
  barGroupConfig?: BarGroupConfig;
  chartFooterConfig?: ChartFooterConfig;

  // Accessibility
  accessibility?: AccessibilityConfig;
}
```

## Props

### Parent Component Props (Layer 2)

| Prop          | Type                                            | Default | Description                                                                 |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `data`        | `ChartSeriesDataPoint[] \| MultiBarDataPoint[]` | `[]`    | Array of data points (canonical or legacy format)                           |
| `seriesOrder` | `string[]`                                      | -       | Control series order for canonical format                                   |
| `width`       | `number \| string`                              | `328`   | Container width                                                             |
| `height`      | `number \| string`                              | `400`   | **Total height of the chart.** VerticalMultiBarGroup fills remaining space. |
| `fullWidth`   | `boolean`                                       | `false` | Stretch chart to fill its parent container width                            |
| `chartHeader` | `boolean`                                       | `true`  | Show chart header                                                           |
| `chartFooter` | `boolean`                                       | `true`  | Show chart footer                                                           |
| `chartLegend` | `boolean`                                       | `true`  | Show chart legend                                                           |
| `dataDisplay` | `boolean`                                       | `false` | Show DataDisplay component above the bar group                              |
| `interactive` | `boolean`                                       | `true`  | Enable hover/click interactivity                                            |
| `animated`    | `boolean`                                       | `false` | Enable entry animation where bars grow from bottom to top on first load     |

### ChartHeader Config (`chartHeaderConfig`)

| Prop                 | Type     | Default     | Description         |
| -------------------- | -------- | ----------- | ------------------- |
| `chartTitleValue`    | `string` | `undefined` | Chart title text    |
| `chartSubtitleValue` | `string` | `undefined` | Chart subtitle text |

### ChartLegend Config (`chartLegendConfig`)

| Prop                         | Type                                                       | Default | Description                                                                                      |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `items`                      | `ChartLegendItem[]`                                        | -       | Manual legend items (overrides auto-generation)                                                  |
| `series1Label`               | `string`                                                   | `""`    | Label for bar series 1 in legend                                                                 |
| `series2Label`               | `string`                                                   | `""`    | Label for bar series 2 in legend                                                                 |
| `series3Label`               | `string`                                                   | `""`    | Label for bar series 3 in legend                                                                 |
| `interactiveDataHead`        | `boolean`                                                  | `false` | When true, legend DataHead values update dynamically on bar hover. Requires `showDataHead: true` |
| `formatHoverSupportingLabel` | `(category: CategoryValue, seriesIndex: number) => string` | -       | Custom formatter for the supporting label text shown on hover                                    |

> **Stable legend width**: When `interactiveDataHead` is enabled, the chart automatically pre-computes all possible hover lead values and supporting label texts from the dataset and passes them to ChartLegend. ChartLegend measures these with the matching font tokens and sets a `minWidth` on each ChartKey's DataLead and SupportingLabel (except the last key), preventing layout shift when hover values change.

### BarGroup Config (`barGroupConfig`)

| Prop                    | Type                                       | Default      | Description                                                                                                                        |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `topLabels`             | `boolean`                                  | `false`      | Show value labels above/below bars                                                                                                 |
| `categoryLabels`        | `boolean`                                  | `true`       | Show category labels at bottom                                                                                                     |
| `yAxis`                 | `boolean`                                  | `true`       | Show the Y-axis                                                                                                                    |
| `avgLine`               | `boolean`                                  | `false`      | Show average line across chart                                                                                                     |
| `valueFormat`           | `ValueFormatConfig`                        | -            | Auto-format for all chart values                                                                                                   |
| `barWidth`              | `string`                                   | `"M"`        | T-shirt sizing: XS, S, M, L, XL, 2XL                                                                                               |
| `hoverType`             | `'group' \| 'individual' \| 'categorical'` | `'group'`    | Hover type: group (cluster highlights), individual (single bar), or categorical (same series across categories)                    |
| `hoverBadge`            | `boolean`                                  | `false`      | Show DataBadge following cursor on hover                                                                                           |
| `yAxisConfig`           | `object`                                   | -            | Y-axis configuration: `{ tickCount?, formatValue?, valueFormat?, yAxisLabel?, yAxisLabelValue?, axisTickSkipper?, skippedTicks? }` |
| `avgLineConfig`         | `object`                                   | -            | Average line configuration: `{ formatValue?, type?, thresholdValue?, dataBadge? }`                                                 |
| `hoverBadgeConfig`      | `object`                                   | -            | Hover badge configuration: `{ formatValue?: function, formatBadge?: function, preset?: HoverBadgePreset }`                         |
| `categoryLabelConfig`   | `CategoryLabelConfig`                      | -            | Category label truncation, overflow grouping, and layout. See sub-table below                                                      |
| `dataSort`              | `DataSortOrder`                            | `"unsorted"` | Sort bars by total absolute value: `"asc"`, `"desc"`, or `"unsorted"` (dataset order)                                              |
| `animated`              | `boolean`                                  | `false`      | Enable entry animation where bars grow from bottom to top on first load                                                            |
| `onBarHover`            | `function`                                 | -            | Callback fired when any bar hover state changes                                                                                    |
| `onBarClick`            | `function`                                 | -            | Callback fired when any bar is clicked                                                                                             |
| `highlightedBarIndices` | `number[]`                                 | -            | Indices of bar-cluster categories rendered at full opacity; every other category dims (multi-cluster highlight)                    |
| `hoveredBarIndex`       | `number \| number[]`                       | -            | Back-compat alias for `highlightedBarIndices`. Accepts single category index or array                                              |

#### `categoryLabelConfig`

Controls truncation, multi-line wrapping, and overflow grouping of category labels. Uses the same shared utilities as VerticalBarChart (`src/utils/categoryLabelUtils.ts`).

| Property                 | Type                                | Default       | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `maxWords`               | `number`                            | `3`           | Maximum words per label before truncation (appends "…")                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| `maxLines`               | `number`                            | `2`           | Maximum display lines per label (CSS `-webkit-line-clamp`)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| `othersLabel`            | `string`                            | `"Others"`    | Label text for the overflow group                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| `overflowType`           | `"grouped" \| "truncated" \| "all"` | `"truncated"` | `"truncated"` (default): bars that don't fit are removed from the right. `"grouped"`: overflow items aggregated into an "Others" multi-bar. `"all"`: every bar is rendered but in-between category labels are skipped to prevent overlap (hovering any bar — including those with hidden labels — reveals the full category name in the HoverBadge and the `onBarHover` callback) |
| `skippedLabels`          | `"auto" \| number`                  | `"auto"`      | Only used when `overflowType` is `"all"`. `"auto"` dynamically calculates which labels to show based on available width. A `number` sets an explicit skip interval (e.g., `1` = every other label)                                                                                                                                                                                |
| `enableOverflowGrouping` | `boolean`                           | `false`       | **Deprecated** — use `overflowType` instead. `true` maps to `"grouped"`, `false` maps to `"truncated"`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| `labelWidth`             | `"fluid" \| number`                 | `"fluid"`     | `"fluid"`: labels expand to fill space with design-token gaps. `number`: fixed pixel width per label                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
| `othersPosition`         | `"sorted" \| "end"`                 | `"sorted"`    | `"sorted"`: positioned by accumulated value. `"end"`: pinned to far right                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| `othersHeight`           | `"relative" \| "full" \| number`    | `"relative"`  | Height mode for the "Others" bar. For multi-bar, "Others" aggregates per-series values from overflow.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |

### ChartFooter Config (`chartFooterConfig`)

| Prop                   | Type     | Default     | Description                     |
| ---------------------- | -------- | ----------- | ------------------------------- |
| `annotationLeftValue`  | `string` | `undefined` | Annotation left text in footer  |
| `annotationRightValue` | `string` | `undefined` | Annotation right text in footer |

### DataDisplay Config (`dataDisplayConfig`)

#### Chart-specific props

| Prop                    | Type                                                                     | Default    | Description                                                          |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `mode`                  | `"static" \| "hover"`                                                    | `"static"` | Display mode: static uses provided values, hover updates dynamically |
| `formatHoverLeadValue`  | `(value: number, category?: CategoryValue, barIndex?: number) => string` | -          | Custom formatter for lead value in hover mode                        |
| `formatHoverBadgeValue` | `(value: number, category?: CategoryValue, barIndex?: number) => string` | -          | Custom formatter for badge value in hover mode                       |

#### DataDisplay Layer 2 props

| Prop                       | Type                        | Default  | Description                                                 |
| -------------------------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| `mainLabelValue`           | `string`                    | -        | The main label text above the data value                    |
| `alignment`                | `"Left" \| "Center"`        | `"Left"` | Layout alignment: horizontal or vertical stacked            |
| `rightBadgeWrapper` | `boolean`                   | `true`   | Toggle visibility of the rightBadgeWrapper section   |
| `badgeTop`                 | `boolean`                   | `false`  | Toggle visibility of the badgeTop slot                      |
| `badgeBottom`              | `boolean`                   | `true`   | Toggle visibility of the badgeBottom slot                   |
| `showBadge`                | `boolean`                   | `true`   | Toggle visibility of the Badge in supporting slots          |
| `supportingBadgeLabel`     | `boolean`                   | `true`   | Toggle visibility of the supporting label next to the badge |
| `supportingBadgeLabelValue`     | `string`                    | -        | The supporting label text next to the badge                 |
| `size`                | `"XS" \| "S" \| "M" \| "L" \| "XL"` | `"L"` | Local size variant for typography scaling              |

#### DataDisplay Layer 3 configs

| Prop                      | Type                      | Default | Description                                                                |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dataHead`    | `DataHeadConfig` | -       | Configuration for the DataHead child component                  |
| `badgeConfig` | `BadgeConfig`    | -       | Configuration for the Badge + SupportingLabel in supporting slots |

## Usage Examples

### Basic Usage (Organized Props)

```tsx
const data = [
  { label: "Q1", value1: 120, value2: 90, value3: 150 },
  { label: "Q2", value1: 100, value2: 110, value3: 130 },
  { label: "Q3", value1: 80, value2: 70, value3: 100 },
  { label: "Q4", value1: 140, value2: 120, value3: 160 },
];

<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: "Quarterly Revenue by Product Line",
    chartSubtitleValue: "Revenue comparison across three product categories",
  }}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    series1Label: "Product A",
    series2Label: "Product B",
    series3Label: "Product C",
  }}
/>;
```

### Full Configuration

```tsx

<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  width={450}
  height={280}
  chartHeader={true}
