## Accessibility

This chart implements the full three-tier ARIA accessibility architecture (see [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) → Chart Accessibility).

### Three-Tier Architecture

| Layer          | Component / Hook                              | Responsibility                                                                                                                                                             |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1. Wrapper** | `ChartAccessibility`                          | `role="figure"`, auto-summary, hidden data table, `aria-live="polite"` region                                                                                              |
| **2. Group**   | `VerticalMultiBarGroup` + `useRovingTabIndex` | Single Tab stop, Arrow/Home/End navigation, `role="group" aria-label="Chart data"`, passes ARIA props to bars                                                              |
| **3. Bar**     | `VerticalMultiBar`                            | `role="button"`, roving `tabIndex`, descriptive `aria-label`, `aria-roledescription="data point"`, `aria-controls`, `data-roving-item`, Enter/Space click, focus/blur sync |

### ARIA Live Region

The chart uses `useChartAccessibility` (which composes `useAriaLiveRegion` internally) to debounce hover/focus announcements (150ms) for screen readers. When a bar is hovered or focused:

```
"Q1, 120, 25.5% of total"
```

The announcement text is passed to `ChartAccessibility` via `liveText`, which renders it in an `aria-live="polite"` region.

### aria-controls Linking

When `dataDisplay={true}`, a stable `dataDisplayId` returned by `useChartAccessibility` links the bars to the DataDisplay region via `aria-controls`. This tells assistive technology that bar interactions update the DataDisplay content.

```
DataDisplay (id={dataDisplayId})  ←  VerticalMultiBar (aria-controls={dataDisplayId})
```

### Keyboard Navigation

| Key                | Action                                          |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `Tab`              | Moves focus to/from the active bar in the group |
| `Arrow Left/Right` | Moves focus to previous/next bar group          |
| `Home / End`       | Moves focus to first/last bar group             |
| `Enter / Space`    | Fires click callback                            |

### Decorative Elements

All decorative elements are `aria-hidden="true"`: YAxis, AvgLine, ZeroLine, HoverBadge.

### Hit Area Extension

`VerticalMultiBarGroup` computes `hitAreaWidth` for each `VerticalMultiBar`, extending the interactive region to fill the gap between bar groups. The hit area is hover-type-aware:

| hoverType       | Behavior                                                                               |
| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `"group"`       | Entire hit area triggers group hover — all bars highlight together                     |
| `"individual"`  | Hit area resolves cursor X to specific bar via `resolveBarFromX`                       |
| `"categorical"` | Same as individual — resolved bar index propagates as `highlightedBarIndex` across all |

See [VerticalMultiBar → Hit Area Extension](./VerticalMultiBar.md#hit-area-extension) and [VerticalMultiBarGroup → Hit Area Extension](./VerticalMultiBarGroup.md#hit-area-extension) for implementation details.

### Accessibility Config (`accessibility`)

| Prop        | Type      | Default | Description                                                       |
| ----------- | --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `enabled`   | `boolean` | `true`  | Enable/disable all accessibility features                         |
| `dataTable` | `boolean` | `true`  | Render a visually-hidden data table for screen readers            |
| `summary`   | `string`  | auto    | Custom summary text (overrides auto-generation)                   |
| `ariaLabel` | `string`  | `title` | Custom aria-label for the chart container (overrides chart title) |

