## Sparse Data Edge Case

When the chart receives only 1-3 data entries, `VerticalMultiBarGroup` automatically renders grey placeholder bars alongside the real data to indicate that more data is expected. The total bar count is always **4** (real + dummy) — `VerticalMultiBarGroup` overrides the shared `sparseDataUtils` default of 5 to keep the sparse fallback tight in grouped multi-bar charts. No additional props are needed — the behavior is automatic.

- **4+ entries**: Normal rendering
- **1-3 entries**: Real bar groups (left) + grey dummy bars (right, count = 5 − real), first dummy matches the tallest bar in the last real group and is labeled "No entries yet"
- **0 entries**: Empty chart

```tsx
// 1 data entry → automatically shows grey placeholder bars
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={[
    { category: "Jan", series: "A", value: 80 },
    { category: "Jan", series: "B", value: 60 },
  ]}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{ chartTitleValue: "Early Data" }}
  barGroupConfig={{ yAxis: true }}
/>
```

See [VerticalMultiBarGroup.md — Sparse Data Edge Case](./VerticalMultiBarGroup.md#sparse-data-edge-case-1-3-entries) and [sparseDataUtils.md](./sparseDataUtils.md) for full details.

